WEBVTT

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.830
It's here!

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.120
I wonder if this Order
is details about the concert.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.580
Probably more outrageous stuff.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.700
Awesome!
Whatever comes, we'll overcome it!

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.910
I wonder what it is?

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.250
Jun? Did something happen?

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.830
Reika?

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.830
What's up? Did something happen?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.040
"DISBAND"

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.540
"Goodbye to Our World"

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.080
Wh-What kind of joke is this?
How ridiculous.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.200
Joke?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.450
It has to be!

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.660
Telling us to disband? I don't get it!

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:39.330
Th-That's right! As if telling us
to disband is really an Order!

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.160
Maybe it's playing a prank on us!

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.330
Man, that's one nasty prank.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.950
It doesn't seem like something it would say.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.080
Has it ever done that?

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.160
Up until now,
has anything the Wall said ever been a joke?

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.000
"DISBAND"

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.950
Th-That sure is some joke
Mr. Wall told us, huh?

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.250
"DISBAND"

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.040
Gouda?

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.040
I'll make the arrangements.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.790
Hey, wait!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.950
Does that mean we're really gonna disband?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.290
Th-There has to be some sort of mistake.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.790
That's right! This is so weird!

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.040
Is the company okay with this?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.500
What about the fans?
What will happen to the fans?

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:56.040
Right! It ain't like the public
will be satisfied with this!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.080
The Wall's Orders are absolute.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.040
Are you insane?

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.830
We've been doing
what the Wall has told us to all this time.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.700
You think we're gonna disband
with a "Yes sir"?

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.620
Are you okay with this?

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:22.330
GIP is a company that was created
to help produce what the Wall wanted.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:28.330
You and all of us in the company
were gathered together for that purpose.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.250
I will make arrangements.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:46.450
N-No way, we can't possibly
be breaking up, right?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:50.370
I told you, it won't come to that.
His dumb joke only gets 30 points.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:57.330
After gathering us together, breaking us up
after a year without waiting, what's the point?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.830
The organization has functioned
on a budget this whole time for expenditures,

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:03.750
so I doubt they've taken this into account.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.500
Seriously!

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.750
What's going to happen to us?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.950
"CANCEL ALL TELEVISION PROGRAMS"

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:44.620
"COMPLETELY CLOSE OFFICE"

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.080
"ANNOUNCE THE DISBANDING"

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.410
"22/7 DISBANDS"

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.790
What? 22/7's disbanding?

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:29.950
Seriously? But why?

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.410
You mean you want us to read it just like this?

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.620
"DISBAND ANNOUNCEMENT
MEMBER COMMENT SCRIPT"

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:45.000
As I told you,
this is another of the Wall's Orders.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.080
--But--
--Well, then...

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.950
...if you could do the honors.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.160
Wai--

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.700
I wonder if I can remember all of this.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.200
"22/7 DISBANDING PRESS CONFERENCE"

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.200
Thank you for gathering on such short notice

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:19.330
and taking time out of your busy day
to come to this meeting.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:24.950
We would now like to begin
this 22/7 disbanding meeting.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:27.450
Tell us details
about what prompted this decision.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.790
Did this come about due to an issue
among the members?

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.830
Or was it an issue internally
within the company at GIP?

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:37.330
Miss Miu Takigawa, you're center.
How do you feel right now?

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:44.120
How do you feel about the accountability
you have towards your fans?

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:48.410
While I cannot give you specifics
about what happened,

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:51.250
I can say this is not the members' fault.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.790
We hope you can understand that.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:57.290
That explanation won't satisfy your fans!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:02.950
A reliable source told me that you're disbanding
due to discord between the members!

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:11.870
Now we'll have the members
greet you all one by one.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:19.500
I wanted to apologize
for all of us causing such concern.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:22.500
From the bottom of our hearts,
we're very sorry.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.620
You think we'll let you
end this with an apology?

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:27.120
Tell us why you're disbanding!

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:30.790
Th-That's...

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:35.910
This is Miyako Kono.
We want to apologize to our fans for this.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.120
I know that if we apologize,
it doesn't necessarily mean we'll be forgiven.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.580
We say this with the intent
of taking criticism seriously.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:47.540
We would appreciate it if you could
understand why we made this decision.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:54.330
We feel morally responsible for disbanding
without fulfilling your hopes and expectations.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:09:01.580
We wish to live our lives with pride
and the love and support you all gave us.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:07.450
We have nothing but gratitude in our hearts for
the support of the fans that helped sustain us.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:10.830
You announced you were going to have
a first anniversary concert in December.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:14.370
Isn't disbanding a complete
stab in the back to your fans?

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:28.080
Thank you so much
for supporting 22/7 all of this time.

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:36.200
We thank you...

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.580
...for supporting us up until now!

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.620
Do you think this will satisfy your fans?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.790
Shouldn't you divulge
the reason why you're disbanding?

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:50.250
Don't you think it's fair
if they see this as a betrayal?

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:58.040
I entered this group with the intent
to do something I didn't want to do.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:01.290
I've become accustomed
to doing things I don't want to do.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.450
Nicole.

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:17.910
With that, this meeting is over.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:19.660
Please, one more shot!

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:21.410
What's your state of mind right now?

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:31.250
22/7 has suddenly and dramatically
announced their disbandment.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.540
Without any sort of explanation whatsoever,

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:36.410
their announcement
has caused rumors to fly about.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:41.580
They abandoned their fans and their feelings
and had a forced announcement of disbanding.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:42.250
According to some reports,

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.000
"RIP HARDCORE FANS #22/7"
"BECAUSE GIP IS JUST GONNA
LOOK THE OTHER WAY. #22/7"

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.000
According to some reports,

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.250
"BECAUSE GIP IS JUST GONNA
LOOK THE OTHER WAY. #22/7"

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.250
it seemed the members
were unwilling to have that meeting at all.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.290
"IS THIS JUST
A DIFFERENCE OF GOALS? #22/7"

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.290
it seemed the members
were unwilling to have that meeting at all.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.250
"LMAO THEY JUST KEEP REFUSING #22/7"

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.250
Perhaps they just weren't
feeling up to the task from the beginning.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.910
"ARE THEY DISAGREEING
WITH THEIR AGENCY? #22/7"

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.910
Perhaps they just weren't
feeling up to the task from the beginning.

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:51.160
"SCANDAL? #22/7"

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:51.160
Day after day, supporting fans
have been asking people to sign petitions.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:54.040
"THE FAULT IS ON THE MEMBERS TOO! #22/7"

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:54.040
Day after day, supporting fans
have been asking people to sign petitions.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:11:00.000
And in front of the GIP office, throngs of
protesting fans have continued to gather.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.290
Ever since the meeting with reporters,
GIP still hasn't released any formal statements.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:13.290
Unfortunately this is goodbye,
my sweet home.

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:16.410
After this,
we won't be returning here anymore.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.540
I'm going ahead.

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.500
Hey, wait, Nicorun!

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.450
At least let us say goodbye.

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:36.450
Nicole was the one who said
that 22/7 was our chance at fame.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:39.700
So she's probably the one
that's the most shocked by all of this.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.870
The Internet's saying harsh things about us.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:49.500
Like this is a scandal, we're apathetic idols,
and whatever else they want to say.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.250
Of course they're saying those things.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:54.830
It's not like we gave them
a satisfying explanation.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:59.160
It's the fans who were cheering us on
that must have felt miserable.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:02.750
I really wanted to do
the one year anniversary concert, too.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:09.290
B-But, you know,
this is all just for right now.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:14.910
The fans will forget all about us,
the idols who had no goals!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:18.910
We were just brought together, after all.

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.750
We...

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:29.910
I wonder if we did anything wrong...

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.870
To get disbanded like this so suddenly...

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:38.700
Did we fail to do something
to keep the Wall happy?

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:41.700
I don't recall going
against anything it told us to do,

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:46.290
and our activities
were going pretty well, but...

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.870
...we had our emotions toyed with.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:58.870
If only we could go back.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:10.620
Disbandment.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.620
It was like Miyako said.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.870
If only we could go back.

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:18.370
It's not something
I started doing because I liked it.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:24.160
But if we have to end things
like this so half-heartedly,

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.660
just why did the Wall
gather us all in the first place?

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.250
Miu Takigawa...

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.870
That's you, right?
I'm Takumi from the "Weekly Buncho."

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.830
From your position as center, could you please
talk to us about your disbandment?

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.370
I have to get away!

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:45.500
Don't you think you owe
your fans some accountability?

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.370
Miss Takigawa!

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:49.450
She's persistent.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.370
Where'd she go?

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.250
Saito?

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:09.700
It's rough being center, huh?

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.700
Because you're in the middle of everything,

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.870
somehow that makes you
the team's representative.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.410
That was careless.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:21.410
Be careful.
Those guys are hanging around the office.

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:24.580
S-Sorry.

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:28.750
Those reporters
will go somewhere else after a bit.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:38.910
So she's probably the one
that's the most shocked by all of this.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:48.120
Saito, what are you going to do?

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:52.080
I know you always wanted to become an idol.

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:54.750
Without 22/7...

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.910
Apparently another agency may pick me up.

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:01.200
Huh?

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.450
That's one good thing, at least.

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:07.120
I can probably pull the 22/7 fans in.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.250
It's a pretty big company.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:11.370
Is that right?

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:12.910
That's amazing.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:22.660
Why did you come to GIP?

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:28.410
Why did you want to become an idol?

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.250
Because someone told me...

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:40.950
...adults do things they don't want to do.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:45.200
And that person was right.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.750
Adults are always selfish.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:51.120
They put our feelings to the side.

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:56.290
And that way,
you become used to all sorts of people.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.580
I don't believe that.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.250
I mean, come on.

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:09.620
Losing something to become thick-skinned
isn't necessarily how you become an adult.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:12.870
In reality, the Wall is inside everyone.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:17.910
Everyone's always living selfishly
at any given time.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.660
Adults are just a later version of kids.
That's all.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:25.450
Or else no one would dream.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.330
Wait!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:35.910
Hey...

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:41.790
What's the thing most precious to you?

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:48.620
Never mind.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.040
See you later.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:10.450
The thing most precious to me?

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.080
I'm home!

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:19.870
Yo!

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:21.870
Big Sister! What's wrong?

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:23.200
Have you really come home?

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.540
What happened to 22/7?

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:29.290
Well, it was a lot of stuff with adults.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:30.450
Miyako!

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:32.160
Mom!

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:36.450
Did you finally become a space cop?

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:42.160
There weren't too many Martians!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.290
Wai--

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.500
What's this?

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.160
What's that?

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.290
What's all this?!

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:06.450
Don't just remodel things like that!

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:08.700
Of course I had to!

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:11.200
This is for all of my cute daughter's goods.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:13.250
You can't live like this!

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.540
No, I'm fine, Father.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:30.410
I'm doing great, actually.

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:32.410
I'm coming home.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:34.950
I promised I would, after all.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:45.290
I know we agreed you could do this
as long as you didn't neglect your studies.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:48.950
It was only supposed to be for a few months.

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:51.450
Hasn't this dragged on for too long?

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.830
Yes.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:55.000
Oh dear, look at the time.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:58.160
If you're going to stay home,
please clean your room, okay?

00:18:58.160 --> 00:18:59.290
Yes.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:11.580
Hoshigawa's newest storyboard was the best!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:15.950
"TERUGAKUKAN EDITOR
TANAKA"

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:15.950
Even though there are idols, it has a very
good sense of reality to it! Very lifelike!

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:18.500
Let's go in this direction
and meet about serialization,

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:22.410
so if you could prepare a storyboard
for the second chapter...

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:23.790
Hello?

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:33.080
♪ I liked you so much
that I told others about it ♪

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:35.750
♪ I was so excited just to
have you at my side ♪

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:39.410
Ever since she came home,
she's been singing nonstop.

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:39.410
♪ I was so excited just to
have you at my side ♪

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:42.040
I wonder if she's
just given up trying to be cheerful.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:42.040
♪ I hid my feelings
so you wouldn't figure it out for so long ♪

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:45.660
♪ I hid my feelings
so you wouldn't figure it out for so long ♪

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.290
♪ I couldn't confess... ♪

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.750
Hey, Jun...

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.330
...shouldn't you take a break?

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:53.580
I have an idea! Let's go somewhere tomorrow!
Been a while since we did that!

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:04.500
But, hey, if you want
to sing for now, that's fine!

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.660
Don't worry! I'm fine!

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:11.160
♪ Don't close the door ♪

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:13.080
♪ Don't slam the door ♪

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:16.830
♪ Leave it but one centimeter open ♪

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:21.000
♪ And as hazy light
vaguely spills through that... ♪

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:24.750
Isn't that 22/7's Jun Toda?

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:26.830
Wow! It really is Jun Toda!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.160
I'm so sorry!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.660
♪ Don't close the door ♪

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.250
♪ Don't slam the door ♪

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:40.330
--Jun.
--♪ Leave it but one centimeter open ♪

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:41.660
♪ And as hazy light... ♪

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:43.200
"AREN'T THE MEMBERS KEEPING SILENT
ABOUT THIS? #22/7"

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:44.790
"I BELIEVED IN THEM... #22/7"

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:46.830
"THIS IS AN ACT OF TREACHERY. #22/7"

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:49.450
Soon everyone will forget all about this!

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.040
"IT ISN'T THE MEMBERS' FAULT."

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.040
"THE MEMBERS MAY WANT TO TALK
ABOUT THEIR REAL FEELINGS, BUT CAN'T."

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:57.500
"GIP IS THE ONE AT FAULT."

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:03.540
We haven't had a say in any of this
since the beginning.

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:07.250
We were idols chosen by the Wall.

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:12.500
We did as we were ordered by the Wall,
and now we're being ordered to leave.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:19.830
"I'VE DECIDED TO SUPPORT THEM FOR LIFE."

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:30.330
My most precious thing?

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:40.200
It's been a month
since that meeting with the reporters,

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:44.040
and in that time, the Wall
hasn't spit out a single Order.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.870
GIP has become an unmanned facility.

00:23:42.080 --> 00:23:45.450
Okay, everyone, take your seats.

00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:46.700
Oh, crap!

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:50.290
We have a transfer student
who will be joining us.

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:55.330
Can you introduce yourself?

00:23:55.330 --> 00:23:57.870
U-Um...

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:03.330
My name is Miu Takigawa...

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:05.450
...and I look forward to learning
with all of you.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:08.700
"Episode 11: Chasing Our Dreams"

00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:11.950
"Episode 11: Chasing Our Dreams"

00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:11.950
"Chasing Our Dreams."
